# Story 79: What Are Humanoids? (50s)
# Hook: An agent that talks to the outside world -- WhatsApp, Slack, email, phone, chat.
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-079-what-are-humanoids.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
An agent that talks to the outside world -- WhatsApp, Slack, email, phone, chat.

[00:03.0 --> 00:09.0]
Launch rysh. A humanoid is an autonomous agent plus bidirectional external communication channels.

[00:09.0 --> 00:16.0]
An inbound message becomes a prompt; the AI reply goes back out through the same channel. Double-Escape into rysh mode to spawn one.

[00:16.0 --> 00:26.0]
Spawn it just like an agent: a name and a system prompt. Use ##humanoid spawn instead of ##agent spawn.

[00:26.0 --> 00:36.0]
##humanoid list shows every humanoid, its status, and which channels it has connected.

[00:36.0 --> 00:47.0]
You can still talk to it directly with the at-sign prefix, exactly like any agent -- channels just add external reach on top.

[00:47.0 --> 00:50.0]
Humanoids: your AI, reachable wherever your users already are.

